# Typed I32 Count-Trailing-Zeros Acceptance

schema_version: 1
directive: `INBOX-37 Part 1`
target: `x86_64-linux`
validation_tier: 3
result: pass

The accepted baseline is `e6c145f7`, report state 443 selected / 233 emitting /
210 failing, captured compiler_rt IR md5
`b0eda7a6427c3084fdf096a68696f19c`, and stage4 pin
`bdee02bc0c7f227c0f11bc9a449df673fe803540`. The production and permanent-test
diff used for validation has sha256
`071bcde5e638e9d6bf419b1a220c3fa72a15951575632393ed486de81fc957f6`.
The current-source ReleaseFast z_llvm has sha256
`a65e48282542d44a3fa901346e54f79590018258413b2c8522e8cfd2fba18665`.

The composed selector admits only the exact `llvm.cttz.i32(i32, i1 immarg)`
shape. Both legal immediate flags are accepted; non-i32 payloads, non-i1
flags, non-literal flags, and literals outside zero/one remain fail-closed.
The lowering reuses the existing zero-defined `ctz_i32_edi_eax` machine and
verifier operation, so zero produces 32 even when the intrinsic flag permits
poison. Permanent selector/encoder/verifier execution covers zero, low and
high single bits, an interior single bit, and all-ones. The exact-form unit
test also exercises both legal flags and an invalid literal.

Fresh report-all advances from 443 selected / 233 emitting / 210 failing to
443 selected / 235 emitting / 208 failing. Exactly the two expected rows emit:

- `compiler_rt.floatunsisf.__floatunsisf`;
- `compiler_rt.floatsisf.__floatsisf`.

No collateral emission is claimed. A structured parser extracted exactly
those two captured bodies, changed only their linkage for the native harness,
and z_llvm emitted one relocation-free ELF object containing exactly the two
global functions. `readelf` and `objdump` confirm the expected symbols,
absence of relocations, and trailing-zero scan sequences. A normal Zig
`_start`, linked with `zig build-exe -fno-lld`, executes 23 precomputed-result
calls across the unsigned and signed conversion rows. Inputs include zero,
single-bit powers, all-ones, mantissa rounding boundaries, signed extrema,
and both signs; every expected float bit pattern matches exactly. The
reference generator is pinned Zig, not a runtime host oracle.

